+# Local catalog import package v2
+
+This document defines the offline SQLite package format consumed by `importPackage()` when `package_type` is `catalog_v2`.
+
+## Required envelope
+
+A package contains `package_type: "catalog_v2"`, `schema_version: 2`, `package_id`, `source_id`, `source_revision`, `market_scope`, `source_snapshot_sha256`, `license_sha256`, `rights_evidence_sha256`, `snapshot_manifest`, `catalog`, `records`, and `package_sha256`.
+
+`snapshot_manifest` must include:
+
+- `upstream_revision` — exact upstream release/commit/API revision;
+- `source_urls` — one or more HTTPS URLs;
+- `source_files` — a map of source-file names to lowercase SHA-256 digests;
+- `license_id` — exactly the license identifier registered for the approved source.
+
+The canonical package digest is SHA-256 over the following object, with object keys sorted recursively and without `package_sha256`:
+
+`{ package_type, schema_version, package_id, source_id, source_revision, market_scope, source_snapshot_sha256, license_sha256, rights_evidence_sha256, snapshot_manifest, catalog, records }`.
+
+Each catalog entity carries `source_record_key`, `record_sha256`, `market_scope`, `applicability_precision`, and `review_status`. Its `record_sha256` is SHA-256 over the canonical entity object excluding only `record_sha256` itself. Imported catalog statuses are restricted to `candidate` or `needs_review`; packages cannot self-approve data.
+
+## Normalized collections and references
+
+The importer processes these collections in order: `brands`, `models`, `generations`, `engines`, `transmissions`, `engine_transmission_pairs`, `ecus`, `configurations`, then `records`.
+
+Relationships use `*_record_key` values, never display-name matching or database-local numeric IDs. Technical records in v2 must use `configuration_record_key` and `ecu_record_key`; `configuration_id` and `ecu_id` are rejected because they are local to one SQLite file.
+
+ECU records preserve optional generation, engine and transmission links. Exact configurations require an explicit engine/transmission pair in the same source revision. A configuration is not returned as verified until its generation, engine, transmission, pair, market/year scope, source rights and any linked ECU all pass the independent review gates.
+
+## Rights and transaction guarantees
+
+The source must already be approved in the local source registry. The registry and source snapshot must explicitly permit commercial use, display, offline caching, bulk reuse and redistribution; all source, license, rights-evidence and snapshot hashes must match. Public search access is not treated as permission for bulk/offline redistribution.
+
+The source snapshot, catalog rows, per-entity provenance evidence, technical records, import items and audit event are committed in one `BEGIN IMMEDIATE` transaction. Any invalid hash, missing reference, rights mismatch, source-key collision or technical-record failure rolls back the whole package. Reimporting the same package hash is idempotent. New source revisions create immutable entity/evidence rows; user garage, history and bookmarks are not overwritten.
+
+The normalized catalog tables remain candidates after import. Source-rights approval is not technical verification. Generic SAE/ISO DTC records remain in `generic_sae_iso_obd2`; VAG-specific DTC records require exact configuration and ECU source-record references.
